      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14132980/assets/67eeabfcff4eb24e14c15691c1c9de746a8870808197739577f7696faeada5bc.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,4,\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,4x+1\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=4$ and *below* the line $y=4x+1.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<4,\\,y<4x+1.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=4$ and $y=4x+1$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\le 4,\\,y\\le 4x+1\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 4,\\,y\\le 4x+1\\}.\n$$",
